    "justification": [
      "Severity-adjusted mean removes stable rater-level level difference \u2014 established Phases 2-4, gap closed on pass2 to ~-0.03 per baseline_refresh.",
      "Held-out even->odd predicts adj_odd with RMSE 0.154 R2 0.967 vs raw 0.370 R2 0.810 vs bayes 1.265 (very poor). Adj is far more predictive of latent quality proxied by held-out severity-adjusted mean.",
      "EB lambda 2.00 implies negligible shrinkage for typical n (median w 0.994, p10 w 0.984). Only games with n<50 see material gain if any; but pass2 has no games <100, so shrinkage even more negligible.",
      "BGG bayes (prior 5.49 lambda 2500) correlates 0.61 with adj and has bias -1.07 vs adj, RMSE 1.27 \u2014 useful for popularity ranking but not defensible quality estimate.",
      "SE varies across n_g (e.g., 0.021 at p10 vs 0.108 at p90) so point estimates must not be treated equally precise \u2014 must weight or show uncertainty in expected-rating regression."
    ],
    "for_RQ2_next_phase": {
      "y": "adj_mean_g (or shrunk variant as sensitivity) as the dependent variable representing game quality net of rater severity.",
      "n_weighting": "Weight RQ2 regression by 1/SE^2 ~ n_g / sigma_e2 or use WLS / include SE as measurement error; or at least report SE and show n_g-weighted vs equal-weighted sensitivity. Do not ignore heteroscedasticity.",
      "bayes_role": "Keep bayes as reference but not as y.",
      "raw_role": "Raw is highly correlated with adj but biased by mean(delta) pool; do not use raw as primary."
    }
